#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0033 expect=noViolation domain=LB
#note "⭐ THE CASE PLAN-unplanned-visit-name-fallback FIXES. LB carries VISITNUM but NO VISIT column; SV carries VISIT = 'UNSCHEDULED 1' for the same VISITNUM. Before the fix the name test read VISIT from the PRIMARY only, the absent column folded to a broadcast \"\" (D34 #3), no marker was found, the visit was judged PLANNED, and since TV holds only PLANNED visits the row was reported -- a false positive on a visit the study explicitly names unscheduled. Testing each name on its own -- contains(upper(VISIT), ...) and contains(upper(SV.VISIT), ...) -- makes the name test see SV's name, so tier 2 does not fire and the rule is silent. (Re-authored 2026-09-28, PLAN-case-fold-missing-d36: the spelling was concat(VISIT, \" \", SV.VISIT) until register D36 made a missing operand poison concat.) ⛔ SDTMIG 3-3 on purpose: SVPRESP does not exist as a variable before 3.4, so tier 2 is the branch that decides and the NAME is the only signal there is. ⚠ This file is the sensitivity arm's target -- drop the SV.VISIT test and it MUST red."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-3
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALB | 99
---

dataset SV label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
col SVUPDES  type=Char label="Description of Unplanned Visit"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 99 | UNSCHEDULED 1 |
---

dataset TV label="Trial Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TV | 1 | SCREENING
CDISCPILOT01 | TV | 2 | BASELINE
---
